-- An `if` without `else` is `⊤` when its condition is false, so its `then`
-- branch must be `⊤` (language.md §12.10, checker-v2.md §34):
-- `if_without_else_not_unit` at the branch — a `String` (6:21) and a
-- number (10:21) — and nothing else, the `if` against its context being
-- silent once the branch has failed.
label c = if c then "yes"


count : Bool → Int
count c = if c then 1
